            "content": "# Design: WebSocket PTY Steering for execd\n\n**Status:** Ready for re-implementation\n**Companion:** [PRD-websocket-pty.md](./PRD-websocket-pty.md)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  execd HTTP server (Gin)                                     │\n│                                                              │\n│  /session/*          CodeInterpretingController              │\n│  /ws/session/:id     SessionWebSocket handler                │\n│                                                              │\n│  runtime.Controller                                          │\n│  ├── bashSessionClientMap  sync.Map[sessionID → *bashSession]│\n│  └── *bashSession                                            │\n│       ├── replayBuffer (1 MiB circular)                      │\n│       ├── broadcast goroutine(s)  ← OS pipe / PTY master     │\n│       ├── per-connection io.Pipe  ← AttachOutput()           │\n│       └── bash process (pipe mode or PTY mode)               │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. New Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `pkg/runtime/replay_buffer.go` | 1 MiB circular replay buffer |\n| `pkg/runtime/replay_buffer_test.go` | Unit tests for replay buffer |\n| `pkg/runtime/bash_session_pty_test.go` | PTY integration tests |\n| `pkg/web/model/session_ws.go` | `ClientFrame` / `ServerFrame` types + error codes |\n| `pkg/web/model/session.go` | Session REST request/response models |\n| `pkg/web/controller/session_ws.go` | `SessionWebSocket` handler |\n| `pkg/web/controller/session_ws_test.go` | WS handler integration tests |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Modified Files\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| `pkg/runtime/types.go` | Add `BashSession` interface; add WS/PTY fields to `bashSession` struct |\n| `pkg/runtime/bash_session.go` | Add `Start`, `StartPTY`, `AttachOutput`, `LockWS/UnlockWS`, `SendSignal`, `ResizePTY`, `IsPTY`, `Done`, `ExitCode`, `WriteStdin`; broadcast goroutines; replay wiring |\n| `pkg/runtime/bash_session_windows.go` | Windows stubs for all new `Controller` methods |\n| `pkg/runtime/ctrl.go` | Add `GetBashSession` (moved to `bash_session.go` for build-tag correctness) |\n| `pkg/web/controller/codeinterpreting.go` | Add `CreateSession`, `RunInSession`, `GetSessionStatus`, `DeleteSession`; validate session before SSE commit |\n| `pkg/web/router.go` | Register `/session/*` and `/ws/session/:id` routes |\n| `go.mod` / `go.sum` | Add `github.com/gorilla/websocket` and `github.com/creack/pty` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Structures\n\n### 4.1 `replayBuffer`\n\n```go\ntype replayBuffer struct {\n    mu    sync.Mutex\n    buf   []byte  // circular storage, capacity = 1 MiB\n    size  int\n    head  int     // next write position (mod size)\n    total int64   // monotonic byte counter (never resets)\n}\n```\n\n- `write(p []byte)` — append bytes, overwrite oldest on overflow\n- `readFrom(offset int64) ([]byte, int64)` — return bytes from offset to total; clamp to oldest if evicted\n- `Total() int64` — mutex-guarded read of `total`\n\n### 4.2 `BashSession` interface\n\n```go\ntype BashSession interface {\n    LockWS() bool\n    UnlockWS()\n    Start() error\n    StartPTY() error\n    IsRunning() bool\n    ExitCode() int\n    WriteStdin(p []byte) (int, error)\n    AttachOutput() (stdout io.Reader, stderr io.Reader, detach func())\n    Done() <-chan struct{}\n    SendSignal(name string)\n    ResizePTY(cols, rows uint16) error\n    IsPTY() bool\n}\n```\n\n### 4.3 `bashSession` struct additions\n\n```go\n// Separate PIDs to prevent run() from clobbering WS shell tracking\ncurrentProcessPid int   // short-lived run() command\nwsPid             int   // long-lived Start/StartPTY shell\n\nreplay       *replayBuffer\nwsConnected  atomic.Bool    // exclusive WS lock\nlastExitCode int\nstdin        io.WriteCloser\ndoneCh       chan struct{}\n\n// Output broadcast\noutMu    sync.Mutex\nstdoutW  *io.PipeWriter  // current per-connection sink; nil when no client\nstderrW  *io.PipeWriter  // nil in PTY mode\n\n// PTY\nisPTY bool\nptmx  *os.File\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Key Design Decisions\n\n### 5.1 Broadcast goroutine pattern (not direct pipe hand-off)\n\n**Problem:** Scanner goroutines block in `Scan()` on the shared OS pipe. When a WS client disconnects, cancelling `ctx` does not unblock `Scan()`. Stale goroutines from the prior connection would still be reading when a new client connects.\n\n**Solution:** `Start()` / `StartPTY()` each launch a **broadcast goroutine** that owns the real OS pipe / PTY master fd. It reads in 32 KiB chunks and:\n1. Always writes to `s.replay`\n2. Writes to `s.stdoutW` / `s.stderrW` (the current per-connection `io.PipeWriter`) if non-nil\n\n`AttachOutput()` creates a fresh `io.Pipe` per connection and swaps in the `PipeWriter`. `detach()` closes the `PipeWriter`, sending EOF to the handler's reader — unblocking it immediately without touching the OS pipe.\n\n**Teardown order in handler:**\n```\ncancel() → detach() → pumpWg.Wait() → UnlockWS()\n```\nThis guarantees no stale goroutine is reading when a new client arrives.\n\n### 5.2 Replay-then-attach ordering\n\n**Invariant:** each output byte must be delivered to the client exactly once.\n\n**Correct order:**\n1. Snapshot replay buffer offset (`replayData, nextOffset = replay.readFrom(since)`)\n2. Call `AttachOutput()` — live pipe sink is now active\n3. Send `replay` frame\n4. Stream live output from pipe\n\n**Why:** bytes produced between snapshot and attach land in the live pipe only (not in the replay snapshot), so no byte appears in both. Reversing steps 1 and 2 causes duplicates.\n\n### 5.3 `os.Pipe` instead of `io.Pipe` for `run()`\n\n`exec.Cmd` internally spawns copy goroutines that write into the pipe after `cmd.Start()` returns. Closing an `io.PipeWriter` immediately after `Start()` causes \"write on closed pipe\" errors in those goroutines. `os.Pipe` uses a kernel buffer: closing the parent-side write fd is safe because the child holds its own fd copy; the reader sees EOF only when the child exits. This eliminates the scan↔Wait deadlock without breaking writes.\n\n### 5.4 Separate `wsPid` and `currentProcessPid`\n\n`run()` (fire-and-forget SSE) and `Start/StartPTY` (WS shell) can run concurrently. Using a single PID field would let `run()` clobber the WS shell's PID, breaking `IsRunning()`, `close()`, and `SendSignal()`. Two separate fields keep the two lifecycles independent.\n\n### 5.5 PTY mode\n\n`StartPTY()` uses `github.com/creack/pty` (`pty.StartWithSize`). The PTY master fd serves as both stdin (write) and stdout+stderr merged (read). Env vars `TERM=xterm-256color`, `COLUMNS=80`, `LINES=24` are injected. `ResizePTY` calls `pty.Setsize` with a `TIOCSWINSZ` ioctl.\n\nIn PTY mode:\n- `stderrW` is nil (stderr is merged into ptmx)\n- `AttachOutput()` returns `stderr = nil`\n- The WS handler skips the stderr pump goroutine\n- `resize` frames are forwarded to `ResizePTY`\n\n### 5.6 WS lock (`wsConnected atomic.Bool`)\n\nOnly one WS client per session at a time. `LockWS()` uses `CompareAndSwap(false, true)`. The lock is released **after** pump goroutines exit (`pumpWg.Wait()`), not on connection close, to prevent a reconnecting client from starting new pumps while stale ones are still running.\n\nLock is also released explicitly in error paths (upgrade failure, `Start()` failure) before returning.\n\n### 5.7 Exit watcher\n\nAfter the bash process exits, the handler:\n1. Sends `{\"type\":\"exit\",\"exit_code\":N}`\n2. Sends a WebSocket `CloseMessage` (normal closure)\n3. Calls `conn.Close()`\n\nThis unblocks `ReadJSON` immediately instead of waiting up to 60 s for the read deadline, eliminating the false \"session already connected\" window during reconnect after process exit.\n\n### 5.8 HTTP 404 before WS upgrade\n\nSession existence is checked **before** `wsUpgrader.Upgrade()`. Once the upgrade handshake completes, HTTP status codes can no longer be sent. Checking first allows returning a clean `404` for unknown sessions.\n\n---\n\n## 6. API Reference\n\n### REST\n\n```\nPOST   /session\n       Body: {\"cwd\": \"/opt/app\"}   (optional)\n       Response: {\"session_id\": \"<uuid>\"}\n\nGET    /session/:sessionId\n       Response: {\"session_id\":\"…\",\"running\":true,\"output_offset\":4096}\n\nPOST   /session/:sessionId/run?since=<offset>\n       Body: {\"code\":\"ls -la\",\"timeout_ms\":30000}\n       Response: SSE stream (stdout/stderr/complete events)\n\nDELETE /session/:sessionId\n       Response: 200 OK\n```\n\n### WebSocket\n\n```\nGET /ws/session/:sessionId?pty=1&since=<offset>\n```\n\n**Connection sequence:**\n```\nClient                          Server\n  |                               |\n  |-- GET /ws/session/:id ------> |\n  |                               | (404 if session missing)\n  |                               | (409 if already connected)\n  |<-- 101 Switching Protocols -- |\n  |                               | [start bash if not running]\n  |                               | [snapshot replay buffer]\n  |                               | [AttachOutput → live pipe active]\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"replay\",...} ---- | (if ?since provided and data available)\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"connected\",...} - |\n  |                               |\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"stdout\",...} ---- | (live output)\n  |-- {\"type\":\"stdin\",\"data\":\"ls\\n\"} -->\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"stdout\",\"data\":\"file1\\n\"} --\n  |-- {\"type\":\"resize\",\"cols\":120,\"rows\":40} -->\n  |-- {\"type\":\"signal\",\"signal\":\"SIGINT\"} -->\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"exit\",\"exit_code\":0} ---\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Implementation Phases\n\n### Phase 0.5 — Replay buffer\n- `replay_buffer.go` + tests\n- Wire `replay.write()` into `run()` stdout/stderr scanners\n- `GET /session/:id` returning `output_offset`\n- `?since=` support on `POST /session/:id/run`\n\n### Phase 1 — WebSocket pipe mode\n- `BashSession` interface in `types.go`\n- `Start()`, `LockWS/UnlockWS`, `AttachOutput`, `Done`, `ExitCode`, `WriteStdin`, `SendSignal` on `bashSession`\n- `session_ws.go` model + controller\n- `GET /ws/session/:id` handler (pipe mode only)\n- 5 WS tests: unknown session, ping/pong, stdin forwarding, replay on connect, exit frame\n\n### Phase 2 — PTY mode\n- Add `github.com/creack/pty` dependency\n- `StartPTY()`, `ResizePTY()`, `IsPTY()` on `bashSession`\n- Wire `?pty=1` in WS handler; skip stderr pump; handle `resize` frames\n- 4 PTY tests: basic execution, resize winsize, ANSI sequences, pipe mode unchanged\n\n### Phase 3 — Hardening (bug fixes from history)\n- Broadcast goroutine pattern replacing direct pipe hand-off (goroutine leak fix)\n- Correct replay-then-attach ordering (duplicate output fix)\n- `os.Pipe` for `run()` (deadlock fix)\n- Separate `wsPid` / `currentProcessPid` (data race fix)\n- Exit watcher `CloseMessage` (reconnect window fix)\n- fd leak fixes (close `stdoutR`/`stderrR` in broadcast goroutines)\n- `commandSnapshot` mutex fix (data race on status poll)\n- Windows build fix (move `GetBashSession` to `!windows` file)\n\n---\n\n## 8. Testing Strategy\n\n| Test | Location | What it covers |\n|------|----------|----------------|\n| Replay buffer unit tests | `replay_buffer_test.go` | write/read, circular eviction, caught-up offset, large gap, concurrent |\n| WS: unknown session | `session_ws_test.go` | HTTP 404 before upgrade |\n| WS: ping/pong | `session_ws_test.go` | application-level keepalive |\n| WS: stdin forwarding | `session_ws_test.go` | stdin → bash → stdout round-trip |\n| WS: replay on connect | `session_ws_test.go` | `?since=0` delivers prior output |\n| WS: exit frame | `session_ws_test.go` | exit frame + conn close on process exit |\n| PTY: basic execution | `bash_session_pty_test.go` | `echo` via PTY |\n| PTY: resize winsize | `bash_session_pty_test.go` | `stty size` reflects resize frame |\n| PTY: ANSI sequences | `bash_session_pty_test.g