            "content": "# PRD: WebSocket PTY Terminal for execd\n\n**Status:** Ready for re-implementation (replaces dropped `tty-fork` branch)\n**Key directive (PR #455 @Pangjiping):** Implement a **separate** WebSocket flow. Do NOT modify the existing `RunInSession` / `bashSession` machinery.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Background\n\n`execd` already provides a stateful bash session API:\n\n| Endpoint | Purpose |\n|----------|---------|\n| `POST /session` | Create a bash session |\n| `POST /session/:id/run` | Fire-and-forget code execution, SSE output stream |\n| `DELETE /session/:id` | Destroy session |\n\nThis API is fire-and-forget: each `/run` call spawns a fresh child process, captures its output, and returns. It cannot support:\n\n- Interactive programs (REPLs, `vim`, `htop`, `ssh`) that need a live terminal\n- Real-time stdin injection while a process is running\n- Full ANSI/cursor-control sequences (PTY echo, colors, progress bars)\n- Persistent shell state across reconnects\n\n## 2. Directive from PR #455\n\n> \"Maybe you should implement a separate WebSocket flow instead of modifying the existing `RunInSession`.\"\n> — @Pangjiping (collaborator)\n\n**This means:**\n- The existing `bashSession` struct, `RunInSession`, and all existing session endpoints are **untouched**\n- The WS PTY feature lives in its own types, its own controller file, and its own router group\n- The two flows share only the session ID namespace (same `sync.Map` store is fine) but have independent lifecycles\n\n## 3. Goals\n\n| # | Goal |\n|---|------|\n| G1 | New `GET /pty/:sessionId` WebSocket endpoint for bidirectional PTY terminal access |\n| G2 | PTY sessions are **independent** of the existing `/session/:id/run` flow — no shared state, no shared structs |\n| G3 | Support both **PTY mode** (full terminal via `/dev/ptmx`, default) and **pipe mode** (plain stdin/stdout/stderr, opt-out) |\n| G4 | Allow clients to **reconnect** and replay missed output via a circular replay buffer |\n| G5 | Zero modifications to existing `bashSession`, `RunInSession`, `CreateSession`, `DeleteSession` |\n| G6 | Windows build must not break (stubs for all new symbols) |\n\n## 4. Non-Goals\n\n- Modifying `POST /session/:id/run` or `bashSession.run()`\n- Client-side terminal emulator\n- Multi-client fan-out (one WS connection per PTY session at a time)\n- Persistent sessions across daemon restarts\n\n## 5. User Stories\n\n**US1 – Interactive terminal**\nAs an agent, I open a WebSocket to `/pty/:id` and get a live bash terminal. I can type commands, see prompts, and interact with programs that require a TTY.\n\n**US2 – Full ANSI output**\nAs a client, I receive raw PTY bytes including ANSI escape codes, cursor movements, and color sequences — identical to a real terminal.\n\n**US3 – Terminal resize**\nAs a client, I send a `resize` frame to update `COLUMNS`/`LINES` so programs like `htop` and `man` lay out correctly.\n\n**US4 – Signal injection**\nAs a client, I send a `signal` frame (e.g. `SIGINT`) to interrupt the running process inside the PTY session.\n\n**US5 – Reconnect with replay**\nAfter a network drop, I reconnect with `?since=<offset>` and receive all output I missed without restarting the session.\n\n**US6 – Pipe mode fallback**\nOn environments where PTY setup is unavailable, I connect with `?pty=0` to get separate stdout/stderr pipes instead of a merged PTY stream.\n\n**US7 – No interference with existing API**\nExisting `/session/:id/run` calls continue to work exactly as before, on the same session ID, without any behavioral change.\n\n## 6. Functional Requirements\n\n### 6.1 New PTY Session Lifecycle (separate from existing `/session`)\n\nThe PTY session is created implicitly on first WebSocket connect, or explicitly via a new REST endpoint:\n\n| Method | Endpoint | Description |\n|--------|----------|-------------|\n| POST | `/pty` | Create a PTY session; returns `session_id` |\n| GET | `/pty/:sessionId` | Get PTY session status + replay buffer offset |\n| DELETE | `/pty/:sessionId` | Terminate and delete PTY session |\n| GET (WS) | `/pty/:sessionId/ws` | WebSocket terminal connection |\n\n> The `/pty` namespace is fully separate from `/session`. A PTY session ID and a bash session ID are independent.\n\n### 6.2 WebSocket Endpoint\n\n`GET /pty/:sessionId/ws[?pty=0][&since=<offset>]`\n\n- HTTP 404 **before** upgrade if session does not exist\n- HTTP 409 **before** upgrade if another client is already connected\n- Default mode: PTY (`?pty=0` opts into pipe mode)\n- `?since=<offset>`: replay missed bytes from that offset on connect\n\n### 6.3 WebSocket Framing Protocol\n\n**Client → Server (JSON):**\n\n| `type` | Fields | Action |\n|--------|--------|--------|\n| `stdin` | `data: string` | Write bytes to bash stdin / PTY master |\n| `signal` | `signal: string` | Send named signal to process group (SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGKILL, SIGQUIT, SIGHUP) |\n| `resize` | `cols: int`, `rows: int` | Resize PTY window (PTY mode only; silently ignored in pipe mode) |\n| `ping` | — | Application-level keepalive |\n\n**Server → Client (JSON):**\n\n| `type` | Fields | Meaning |\n|--------|--------|---------|\n| `connected` | `session_id`, `mode: \"pty\"\\|\"pipe\"` | First frame after upgrade |\n| `replay` | `data: string`, `offset: int64` | Missed output since requested offset |\n| `stdout` | `data: string`, `timestamp: int64` | Live output chunk (PTY: merged; pipe: stdout only) |\n| `stderr` | `data: string`, `timestamp: int64` | Live stderr (pipe mode only) |\n| `exit` | `exit_code: int` | Shell process exited |\n| `pong` | — | Response to application-level ping |\n| `error` | `error: string`, `code: string` | Error frame |\n\n**Error codes:**\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `SESSION_GONE` | Session deleted while connected |\n| `START_FAILED` | Failed to start bash process |\n| `STDIN_WRITE_FAILED` | Write to stdin failed |\n| `INVALID_FRAME` | Unknown frame type |\n| `ALREADY_CONNECTED` | Another client holds the WS lock |\n| `RUNTIME_ERROR` | Internal read/write error |\n\n### 6.4 Keepalive\n\n- RFC 6455 binary ping every 30 s; 60 s read deadline reset on pong\n- Application-level `ping`/`pong` frames in parallel\n\n### 6.5 Reconnect Semantics\n\n1. Client disconnects; PTY bash process stays alive\n2. Output continues accumulating in the replay buffer\n3. Client reconnects with `?since=<last_offset>`\n4. Server sends `replay` frame with all missed bytes, then streams live output\n5. Each byte is delivered **exactly once** — no duplicates, no gaps\n\n### 6.6 Output Delivery\n\n- Raw byte chunks (not line-buffered) — PTY prompts and control sequences delivered immediately\n- Chunk size: up to 32 KiB per read\n- Replay buffer: 1 MiB circular; oldest bytes evicted when full\n- Output written to replay buffer **before** fanout to the active WS connection\n\n### 6.7 Constraints from PR review\n\nThe following bugs from the dropped branch must **not** be reproduced:\n\n| Bug | Constraint |\n|-----|-----------|\n| Goroutine leak on disconnect | Pump goroutines must exit before `UnlockWS()` is called |\n| Duplicate output on reconnect | Snapshot replay buffer **before** `AttachOutput()`, not after |\n| WS lock not released on upgrade failure | Release lock in all error paths before returning |\n| WS lock not released on `Start()` failure | Release lock explicitly before error return |\n| `run()` scan↔Wait deadlock | Use `os.Pipe` (not `io.Pipe`) for `run()` — but this is in the existing flow, not our concern |\n| PTY `Setpgid+Setsid` EPERM | Do NOT set `Setpgid` when using `pty.StartWithSize` (it sets `Setsid` internally) |\n| `running` status wrong | Derive from live PID, not `started` bool |\n| fd leaks | Close all pipe read/write ends when no longer needed |\n\n## 7. Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `GET /pty/:id/ws` upgrades to WS and delivers `connected` frame with `mode:\"pty\"`\n- [ ] Typing in stdin appears as output from bash\n- [ ] ANSI escape sequences present in stdout frames (PTY mode)\n- [ ] `resize` frame changes PTY dimensions (verified via `stty size` inside bash)\n- [ ] `signal` SIGINT interrupts a running command\n- [ ] Disconnect + reconnect with `?since=0` delivers all prior output exactly once, no duplicates\n- [ ] `?pty=0` delivers separate stdout/stderr frames\n- [ ] Existing `POST /session/:id/run` behavior is completely unchanged\n- [ ] `go test -race ./...` passes with no data-race reports\n- [ ] `GOOS=windows go build ./...` succeeds\n",
