            "content": "# Design: WebSocket PTY Terminal for execd\n\n**Status:** Ready for re-implementation\n**Companion:** [PRD-websocket-pty.md](./PRD-websocket-pty.md)\n**Key constraint:** Zero modifications to existing `bashSession`, `RunInSession`, or any `/session/*` code.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  execd HTTP server (Gin)                                         │\n│                                                                  │\n│  EXISTING (untouched)          NEW                               │\n│  ─────────────────────         ──────────────────────────────    │\n│  /session/*                    /pty/*                            │\n│    CreateSession                 CreatePTYSession                │\n│    RunInSession (SSE)            GetPTYSessionStatus             │\n│    DeleteSession                 DeletePTYSession                │\n│                                  PTYSessionWebSocket (WS)        │\n│                                                                  │\n│  runtime.Controller                                              │\n│  ├── bashSessionClientMap   (existing, untouched)                │\n│  └── ptySessionMap          (NEW: sync.Map[id → *ptySession])    │\n│       └── *ptySession                                            │\n│            ├── replayBuffer  (1 MiB circular)                    │\n│            ├── broadcast goroutine  ← PTY master / OS pipes      │\n│            ├── per-connection io.Pipe  ← AttachOutput()          │\n│            └── bash process  (PTY mode or pipe mode)             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. New Files (nothing existing is modified)\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `pkg/runtime/pty_session.go` | `ptySession` struct + all methods; build tag `!windows` |\n| `pkg/runtime/pty_session_windows.go` | Windows stubs for all new `Controller` methods |\n| `pkg/runtime/pty_session_test.go` | Unit + integration tests for PTY session |\n| `pkg/runtime/replay_buffer.go` | 1 MiB circular replay buffer (shared utility) |\n| `pkg/runtime/replay_buffer_test.go` | Replay buffer unit tests |\n| `pkg/web/model/pty.go` | REST request/response models for `/pty/*` |\n| `pkg/web/model/pty_ws.go` | `ClientFrame` / `ServerFrame` types + WS error codes |\n| `pkg/web/controller/pty_controller.go` | REST handlers: Create, Status, Delete |\n| `pkg/web/controller/pty_ws.go` | `PTYSessionWebSocket` handler |\n| `pkg/web/controller/pty_ws_test.go` | WS handler integration tests |\n\n**Modified files (minimal):**\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `pkg/runtime/ctrl.go` | Add `ptySessionMap sync.Map`; add `CreatePTYSession`, `GetPTYSession`, `DeletePTYSession`, `GetPTYSessionStatus`, `ReplayPTYOutput` methods |\n| `pkg/web/router.go` | Register `/pty/*` and `/pty/:id/ws` routes |\n| `go.mod` / `go.sum` | Add `github.com/gorilla/websocket` and `github.com/creack/pty` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Structures\n\n### 3.1 `replayBuffer`\n\n```go\n// pkg/runtime/replay_buffer.go\ntype replayBuffer struct {\n    mu    sync.Mutex\n    buf   []byte // circular, capacity = 1 MiB\n    size  int\n    head  int   // next write position (mod size)\n    total int64 // monotonic byte counter\n}\n\nfunc (r *replayBuffer) write(p []byte)\nfunc (r *replayBuffer) Total() int64                          // mutex-guarded\nfunc (r *replayBuffer) readFrom(offset int64) ([]byte, int64) // clamps to oldest if evicted\n```\n\n### 3.2 `ptySession` struct\n\n```go\n// pkg/runtime/pty_session.go  (build tag: !windows)\ntype ptySession struct {\n    id      string\n    cwd     string\n    mu      sync.Mutex\n    closing bool\n\n    // Process tracking\n    pid          int            // PID of the running bash process (0 = not running)\n    lastExitCode int            // -1 until first exit\n    doneCh       chan struct{}   // closed when process exits\n\n    // Stdin\n    stdin io.WriteCloser // pipe write end (pipe mode) or PTY master (PTY mode)\n\n    // PTY\n    isPTY bool\n    ptmx  *os.File // PTY master fd; nil in pipe mode\n\n    // Replay\n    replay *replayBuffer\n\n    // WS exclusive lock\n    wsConnected atomic.Bool\n\n    // Output broadcast (guards stdoutW / stderrW)\n    outMu   sync.Mutex\n    stdoutW *io.PipeWriter // current per-connection sink; nil when no client attached\n    stderrW *io.PipeWriter // nil in PTY mode\n}\n```\n\n### 3.3 `PTYSession` interface (exposed to controller)\n\n```go\ntype PTYSession interface {\n    LockWS() bool\n    UnlockWS()\n    StartPTY() error          // launch bash via pty.StartWithSize\n    StartPipe() error         // launch bash with os.Pipe stdin/stdout/stderr\n    IsRunning() bool          // true iff pid != 0\n    IsPTY() bool\n    ExitCode() int\n    WriteStdin(p []byte) (int, error)\n    AttachOutput() (stdout io.Reader, stderr io.Reader, detach func())\n    Done() <-chan struct{}\n    SendSignal(name string)\n    ResizePTY(cols, rows uint16) error\n    ReplayBuffer() *replayBuffer\n}\n```\n\n### 3.4 REST models\n\n```go\n// pkg/web/model/pty.go\ntype CreatePTYSessionRequest struct {\n    Cwd string `json:\"cwd,omitempty\"`\n}\ntype CreatePTYSessionResponse struct {\n    SessionID string `json:\"session_id\"`\n}\ntype PTYSessionStatusResponse struct {\n    SessionID    string `json:\"session_id\"`\n    Running      bool   `json:\"running\"`   // derived from pid != 0\n    OutputOffset int64  `json:\"output_offset\"`\n}\n```\n\n### 3.5 WS frame models\n\n```go\n// pkg/web/model/pty_ws.go\ntype ClientFrame struct {\n    Type   string `json:\"type\"`\n    Data   string `json:\"data,omitempty\"`\n    Cols   int    `json:\"cols,omitempty\"`\n    Rows   int    `json:\"rows,omitempty\"`\n    Signal string `json:\"signal,omitempty\"`\n}\ntype ServerFrame struct {\n    Type      string `json:\"type\"`\n    SessionID string `json:\"session_id,omitempty\"`\n    Mode      string `json:\"mode,omitempty\"`\n    Data      string `json:\"data,omitempty\"`\n    Offset    int64  `json:\"offset,omitempty\"`\n    ExitCode  *int   `json:\"exit_code,omitempty\"`\n    Error     string `json:\"error,omitempty\"`\n    Code      string `json:\"code,omitempty\"`\n    Timestamp int64  `json:\"timestamp,omitempty\"`\n}\nconst (\n    WSErrCodeSessionGone      = \"SESSION_GONE\"\n    WSErrCodeStartFailed      = \"START_FAILED\"\n    WSErrCodeStdinWriteFailed = \"STDIN_WRITE_FAILED\"\n    WSErrCodeInvalidFrame     = \"INVALID_FRAME\"\n    WSErrCodeAlreadyConnected = \"ALREADY_CONNECTED\"\n    WSErrCodeRuntimeError     = \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Design Decisions\n\n### 4.1 Complete separation from existing `bashSession`\n\n`ptySession` is a new, independent type in `pkg/runtime/pty_session.go`. It does not embed or extend `bashSession`. The `Controller` gets a new `ptySessionMap sync.Map` alongside the existing `bashSessionClientMap`. No existing method signatures change.\n\n### 4.2 Broadcast goroutine pattern\n\n`StartPTY()` / `StartPipe()` each launch a **broadcast goroutine** that owns the real OS fd (PTY master or `os.Pipe` read end). It reads in 32 KiB chunks and:\n\n1. Always writes to `s.replay` first\n2. Then writes to `s.stdoutW` / `s.stderrW` (the current per-connection `io.PipeWriter`) if non-nil\n\n`AttachOutput()` creates a fresh `io.Pipe` per connection and atomically swaps in the writer. `detach()` closes the writer, sending EOF to the handler's reader — unblocking pump goroutines immediately without touching the OS fd.\n\nThis eliminates the goroutine-leak bug from the dropped branch where `bufio.Scanner` goroutines outlived the WS connection.\n\n### 4.3 Replay-then-attach ordering (no duplicates)\n\n```\n1. snapshot = replay.readFrom(since)   // watermark captured\n2. stdout, stderr, detach = AttachOutput()  // live sink now active\n3. send replay frame (snapshot bytes)\n4. stream live from stdout/stderr readers\n```\n\nBytes produced between steps 1 and 2 land in the live pipe only (not in the snapshot), so each byte is delivered exactly once. Reversing steps 1 and 2 causes duplicates — a bug present in the dropped branch that must not recur.\n\n### 4.4 `os.Pipe` for process I/O\n\nUse `os.Pipe()` (kernel-buffered) not `io.Pipe()` (goroutine-coupled) for the bash process's stdin/stdout/stderr in pipe mode. After `cmd.Start()`, close the parent-side write ends immediately — the child holds its own fd copies, so the reader sees EOF only when the child exits. This avoids the scan↔Wait deadlock.\n\n### 4.5 PTY: no `Setpgid`\n\n`pty.StartWithSize` internally sets `Setsid=true`. Combining `Setsid+Setpgid` causes `EPERM` (setpgid is illegal for a session leader). Do **not** set `cmd.SysProcAttr.Setpgid = true` in `StartPTY()`. After `setsid()`, `pgid == pid` automatically, so `Kill(-pid, sig)` in `SendSignal` still works.\n\n### 4.6 WS exclusive lock\n\n`wsConnected atomic.Bool` — `LockWS()` uses `CompareAndSwap(false, true)`. The lock is released **after** pump goroutines exit (`pumpWg.Wait()`), not on connection close. This prevents a reconnecting client from starting new pumps while stale ones are still running.\n\nLock must be released explicitly in **all** error paths:\n- Upgrade failure → `session.UnlockWS()` before return\n- `StartPTY()` / `StartPipe()` failure → `session.UnlockWS()` before return\n\n### 4.7 Exit watcher closes connection immediately\n\nAfter the bash process exits:\n1. Send `{\"type\":\"exit\",\"exit_code\":N}`\n2. Send WebSocket `CloseMessage` (normal closure)\n3. Call `conn.Close()`\n\nThis unblocks `ReadJSON` immediately instead of waiting up to 60 s for the read deadline, eliminating the false \"session already connected\" window during reconnect after process exit.\n\n### 4.8 HTTP 404 before upgrade\n\nCheck session existence **before** `wsUpgrader.Upgrade()`. Once the upgrade handshake completes, HTTP status codes can no longer be sent.\n\n### 4.9 `Running` status from live PID\n\n`GetPTYSessionStatus` derives `Running` from `session.pid != 0`, not from a `started` bool. This accurately reflects whether the process is alive, not just whether it was ever started.\n\n---\n\n## 5. WS Handler Flow\n\n```\nPTYSessionWebSocket():\n  1. Look up ptySession by ID → 404 if missing\n  2. session.LockWS()         → 409 if already locked\n  3. wsUpgrader.Upgrade()     → on fail: UnlockWS(), return\n  4. if !session.IsRunning():\n       if ?pty=0: session.StartPipe() else: session.StartPTY()\n       on fail: send error frame, UnlockWS(), return\n  5. snapshot = replay.readFrom(?since)   // step A: snapshot first\n  6. stdout, stderr, detach = AttachOutput()  // step B: attach second\n  7. defer: cancel() → detach() → pumpWg.Wait() → UnlockWS()\n  8. if snapshot: send replay frame\n  9. send connected frame (mode from session.IsPTY())\n  10. start RFC 6455 ping goroutine (30s interval)\n  11. pumpWg.Add(1); go streamPump(stdout, \"stdout\")\n  12. if stderr != nil: pumpWg.Add(1); go streamPump(stderr, \"stderr\")\n  13. go exitWatcher()  // sends exit frame + CloseMessage + conn.Close()\n  14. read loop: ReadJSON → dispatch stdin/signal/resize/ping frames\n```\n\n`streamPump` reads raw 32 KiB chunks (not line-scanned) and writes `ServerFrame` JSON to the WS connection. Exits on `io.EOF` or `ctx.Done()`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. API Reference\n\n### REST\n\n```\nPOST   /pty\n       Body: {\"cwd\": \"/opt/app\"}   (optional)\n       201: {\"session_id\": \"<uuid>\"}\n\nGET    /pty/:sessionId\n       200: {\"session_id\":\"…\",\"running\":true,\"output_offset\":4096}\n       404: session not found\n\nDELETE /pty/:sessionId\n       200: {}\n       404: session not found\n```\n\n### WebSocket\n\n```\nGET /pty/:sessionId/ws?pty=0&since=<offset>\n    pty=0   → pipe mode (default: PTY mode)\n    since   → replay from this byte offset\n```\n\n**Connection sequence:**\n```\nClient                              Server\n  |                                   |\n  |-- GET /pty/:id/ws ------------->  |\n  |                                   | 404 if session missing\n  |                                   | 409 if already connected\n  |<-- 101 Switching Protocols -----  |\n  |                                   | [StartPTY or StartPipe if not running]\n  |                                   | [snapshot replay buffer]\n  |                                   | [AttachOutput → live pipe active]\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"replay\",...} -------  | (if ?since and data available)\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"connected\",\"mode\":\"pty\",...}\n  |                                   |\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"stdout\",\"data\":\"$ \"}  | (PTY prompt)\n  |-- {\"type\":\"stdin\",\"data\":\"ls\\n\"} >|\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"stdout\",\"data\":\"...\"}  |\n  |-- {\"type\":\"resize\",\"cols\":120,\"rows\":40}\n  |-- {\"type\":\"signal\",\"signal\":\"SIGINT\"}\n  |<-- {\"type\":\"exit\",\"exit_code\":0}  |\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Implementation Phases\n\n### Phase 1 — Replay buffer\n- `pkg/runtime/replay_buffer.go` + `replay_buffer_test.go`\n- 5 tests: write/read, circular eviction, caught-up offset, large gap, concurrent\n\n### Phase 2 — PTY session core\n- `pkg/runtime/pty_session.go`: `ptySession` struct, `StartPTY()`, `StartPipe()`, `AttachOutput()`, `LockWS/UnlockWS`, `WriteStdin`, `SendSignal`, `ResizePTY`, `IsPTY`, `IsRunning`, `ExitCode`, `Done`\n- `pkg/runtime/pty_session_windows.go`: stubs\n- Wire `ptySessionMap` into `Controller` in `ctrl.go`\n- `pkg/runtime/pty_session_test.go`: PTY basic execution, resize, ANSI sequences, pipe mode, reconnect replay\n\n### Phase 3 — REST endpoints\n- `pkg/web/model/pty.go`\n- `pkg/web/controller/pty_controller.go`: `CreatePTYSession`, `GetPTYSessionStatus`, `DeletePTYSession`\n- Register `/pty` routes in `router.go`\n\n### Phase 4 — WebSocket handler\n- `pkg/web/model/pty_ws.go`\n- `pkg/web/controller/pty_ws.go`: `PTYSessionWebSocket`\n- `pkg/web/controller/pty_ws_test.go`: unknown session (404), already connected (409), ping/pong, stdin forwarding, replay on reconnect, exit frame, PTY resize\n- Register `/pty/:id/ws` route in `router.go`\n\n---\n\n## 8. Testing Strategy\n\n| Test | File | Covers |\n|------|------|--------|\n| Replay buffer: write/read | `replay_buffer_test.go` | basic round-trip |\n| Replay buffer: circular eviction | `replay_buffer_test.go` | oldest bytes overwritten |\n| Replay buffer: caught-up offset | `replay_buffer_test.go` | returns nil when current |\n| Replay buffer: large gap | `replay_buffer_test.go` | clamps to oldest available |\n| Replay buffer: concurrent | `replay_buffer_test.go` | race-free under `-race` |\n| PTY: basic execution | `pty_session_test.go` | `echo` via PTY |\n| PTY: resize winsize | `pty_session_test.go` | `stty size` reflects resize |\n| PTY: ANSI sequences | `pty_session_test.go` | escape codes in output |\n| PTY: pipe mode | `pty_session_test.go` | separate stdout/stderr |\n| PTY: reconnect replay | `pty_session_test.go` | AttachOutput after disconnect |\n| WS: 404 before upgrade | `pty_ws_test.go` | unknown session |\n| WS: 409 already connected | `pty_ws_test.go` | concurrent connect |\n| WS: ping/pong | `pty_ws_test.go` | application keepalive |\n| WS: stdin forwarding | `pty_ws_test.go` | stdin → bash → stdout |\n| WS: replay on reconnect | `pty_ws_test.go` | `?since=0` exact-once delivery |\n| WS: exit frame + close | `pty_ws_test.go` | immediate unblock on exit |\n| WS: resize frame | `pty_ws_test.go` | PTY winsize updated |\n\nAll tests run with `-race`.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Dependencies\n\n| Package | Version | Use |\n|---------|---------|-----|\n| `github.com/gorilla/websocket` | v1.5.x | WebSocket upgrade + framing |\n| `github.com/creack/pty` | v1.1.24 | PTY start (`pty.StartWithSize`) + resize (`pty.Setsize`) |\n",
